\section{Model and problem formulation}
\label{sec:system}

This section formalizes client-side ABR at the chunk timescale.
We assume a single client, exogenous trace throughput \(C^{\mathrm{tr}}_k\) at chunk index \(k\), and deterministic buffer updates given \((s_k,a^{\mathrm{exec}}_k,C^{\mathrm{tr}}_k)\), where \(s_k\) is the client state and \(a^{\mathrm{exec}}_k\) the executed ladder rung (\tabref{tab:notation}).
Here, deterministic means that the same inputs always yield the same next buffer and the same executed rung.
Cross-layer scheduling and transport adaptation are out of scope.
Certification of the conformal throughput lower bound is probabilistic (Section~\ref{sec:method}).
