Logged QoE (Equation~\eqref{eq:qoe-rep}) uses \(\mu{=}1.0\) per absolute VMAF-point change and \(\beta{=}4.3\) per stall second throughout the shared simulator; with \(\beta{=}4.3\), one stall second costs only 4.3 VMAF points.
One VMAF point is a small fraction of typical adjacent-rung and top-rung gaps on our ladders in \tabref{tab:ladder:spacing} and is conservative relative to perceptually aware per-title encoding practice~\cite{menon2022perceptual}. It is an engineering design choice aligned with Equation~\eqref{eq:knee}, not a preregistered clinical equivalence margin~\cite{lakens2017equivalence}. Because the knee rule and this TOST both use the session-mean ladder, alignment of the session-mean VMAF change with \(\pm\varepsilon\) is expected; Section~\ref{sec:eval:perchunk} therefore validates budget adherence independently on true per-chunk VMAF.
The scalar in Equation~\eqref{eq:qoe-rep} is only the logging definition. Only the co-design sweep uses the linear score \(\mathrm{QoE}(w)\) defined in Section~\ref{sec:eval:codesign}.
The \(p\)-values we quote for the primary arms are raw and two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank tests with zero-method \texttt{zsplit}.
When bitrate and rebuffering share the same signed-rank statistic on a host---for example, greedy certified--safety \(p{=}\CPSGreedyPBWcs\) for both---the identity is mechanical, not a reporting error.
The co-design values \(\CPScoPVM\) and \(\CPScoPReb\) equal \(1/20{,}000\), the floor of a \(20{,}000\)-draw sign-flip test; they are not Wilcoxon tail probabilities.
The bootstrap intervals in Section~\ref{sec:eval:codesign} are the magnitude statement for that contrast.
For the eight primary certified--safety bitrate and rebuffering contrasts across four non-learned hosts, the largest raw \(p\) is \(\CPSGreedyPBWcs\); all eight remain below the Holm--Bonferroni threshold at family-wise \(0.05\).
One caveat concerns content diversity. Each episode is one \((\text{video},\text{trace})\) pair: the video is drawn uniformly from the twelve titles and the trace from the held-out pool. Observations therefore cluster by title, and effective independent-content diversity is twelve, not \(\CPSepisodes\). We treat the reported \(p\)-values as within-pair evidence on that paired design, not as evidence from \(204\) independent titles.

\subsection{Model-agnostic banking on \mbox{5G} (RQ1--RQ2)}
\label{sec:eval:main}

\tabref{tab:cps:full} reports absolute metrics for all three arms---\textsc{Raw}, \textsc{Safety}, and \textsc{Certified}---on the primary \mbox{5G} test traces for five host families: greedy, BBA, BOLA, RobustMPC, and a Pensieve-style negative control.
The table lists the episode means and significance tests for every arm.
Banking behaves consistently across all four non-learned hosts on the twelve-title suite. Relative to \textsc{Safety}, the \textsc{Certified} arm saves 4.5\%, 4.1\%, 4.1\%, and 3.8\% bitrate on greedy, BBA, BOLA, and RobustMPC, respectively, and reduces rebuffering by 9.3\%, 8.9\%, 8.9\%, and 9.2\% (greedy rebuffering Wilcoxon \(p{=}\CPSGreedyPRebCs\)).
\figref{fig:cps:overview} summarizes only the \textsc{Certified}-vs.-\textsc{Safety} contrast and omits \textsc{Raw}.
On steep, non-saturated ladders the absolute savings stay modest. This is what the mechanism predicts: banking pays off only where the ladder saturates. Every host nevertheless remains perceptually near-lossless.
Partitioning the greedy certified--safety contrast by session-mean top-rung VMAF gain makes that dependence explicit (\tabref{tab:ladder:spacing}). On titles with top gain at most \(2\) VMAF points---Big Buck Bunny, Sintel, Sunflower, and Kristen \& Sara, \(n{=}60\) episodes---banking saves \(4.6\%\) bitrate and \(9.9\%\) rebuffering. On steep titles with top gain at least \(9\)---Park Joy, Ducks Take Off, and Into Tree, \(n{=}51\)---the same contrast shrinks to \(2.1\%\) bitrate and \(3.7\%\) rebuffering. The pooled greedy headline therefore mixes both regimes rather than reflecting a saturation-only subset, saving 4.5\% bitrate and 9.3\% rebuffering.
Mean VMAF differences are perceptually negligible, at \(\CPSGreedyVMcs\), \(\CPSBbaVMcs\), \(\CPSBolaVMcs\), and \(\CPSMpcVMcs\) points across greedy, BBA, BOLA, and RobustMPC, with every value inside \(\pm\varepsilon\) by TOST.


Safety and banking contribute differently. On greedy, mean rebuffering per \(\sim\!192\,\mathrm{s}\) episode of \(48\) chunks falls from \(\CPSGreedyRawReb\)\,s for \textsc{Raw} to \(\CPSGreedySafReb\)\,s for \textsc{Safety} and \(\CPSGreedyCertReb\)\,s for \textsc{Certified}. Against \textsc{Raw}, certified greedy reduces rebuffering by 55.5\%, versus 51.0\% for BBA. Conformal safety removes most of the stall time relative to \textsc{Raw}; banking adds the certified--safety margin on top.
\figref{fig:cps:tradeoff} and \figref{fig:cps:cdf} show per-episode operating points and rebuffering Cumulative Distribution Functions (CDFs) for greedy and BBA.

Coverage follows a distinct pattern on the primary \mbox{5G} pool.
The inclusive empirical coverage---averaging every chunk, including the \(W_{\mathrm{calib}}\) fallback warm-up---is \(\CPSGreedyCov\) for greedy and \(\CPSBbaCov\) for BBA against a \(\CPScovTarget\) target.
On the greedy certified arm, warm-up chunks alone cover at \(\CPSGreedyCovWarm\) and post--warm-up chunks at \(\CPSGreedyCovPost\), so the headline value \(\CPSGreedyCov\) is not a pure finite-sample certificate rate.
Because coverage depends on the throughput trace and the conformal calibrator rather than the base policy, the inclusive rate equals \(\CPSGreedyCov\) across every host and shield variant on the \mbox{5G} test set; see \figref{fig:cps:coverage}.
Proposition~\ref{prop:feas} is a per-chunk probabilistic certificate, not a per-episode stall-free one. On the greedy certified arm we attribute every second of residual rebuffering on the primary \mbox{5G} pool of \(\CPSepisodes\) paired episodes to an exclusive cause. When the residual window is shorter than the conformal warm-up of \(W_{\mathrm{calib}}{=}20\), \(\CPSGreedyStallColdPct\%\) of that stall time occurs; the bound then uses the fixed fallback scale and is not the finite-sample certificate. After warm-up, \(\CPSGreedyStallMissPct\%\) of residual stall time falls on chunks where realized throughput misses its conformal lower bound. A further \(\CPSGreedyStallHeldPct\%\) falls on chunks where the bound holds, matching Proposition~\ref{prop:feas}. The \(B_k\le B_{\mathrm{crit}}\) emergency path contributes \(\CPSGreedyStallEmergPct\%\) of stall seconds on this suite.
\textsc{Safety} still leaves mean rebuffering of \(\CPSGreedySafReb\,\mathrm{s}\) on a \(\sim\!192\,\mathrm{s}\) greedy episode, against \(\CPSGreedyRawReb\,\mathrm{s}\) for \textsc{Raw}; most of the residual certified stall mass sits in the warm-up path above.
Pensieve, the negative control, degrades to near-floor bitrates with near-zero stalls, so CPS rarely intervenes. Banking cannot rescue a policy that never requested saturated rungs.



Greedy proposes the top rung every time, so nearly every banking downshift or feasibility repair appears as an intervention; its intervention rate in \tabref{tab:cps:full} is therefore high. The rate gauges how far a host sits from the certified operating point, not how much of the outcome to attribute to the shield. This is why we run the model-agnostic contrast across hosts spanning the spectrum.

The certified intervention rate falls as the host becomes more conservative: \(\CPSGreedyCertInt\%\) for greedy, \(\CPSBbaCertInt\%\) for BBA, \(\CPSBolaCertInt\%\) for BOLA, \(\CPSMpcCertInt\%\) for RobustMPC, and \(\CPSPenCertInt\%\) for the Pensieve-style host. The sharper the base policy, the lighter the shield's load. Coverage nevertheless holds at \(\CPSGreedyCov\) throughout. The certified metrics therefore depend increasingly on the base policy's own decisions, and the shield acts only where banking headroom remains. For RQ1 and RQ2 the message is simple: on every non-learned host, banking saves bitrate and cuts rebuffering with mean VMAF inside \(\pm\varepsilon\).
Inclusive coverage meets \(\CPScovTarget\) on the primary \mbox{5G} pool; the post--warm-up rate \(\CPSGreedyCovPost\) is the closer operational check of the finite-sample certificate.

